<overview>
<p>Clan foot squads are squad-strength formations of Clan conventional infantry operating outside the standard five-warrior Point structure. These smaller elements serve specialized security roles, observation posts, and detachment duties where a full Point is unnecessary or unavailable. Drawn from the same garrison pool as standard foot Points, squad-sized Clan infantry fills the gaps in territorial defense that larger formations cannot economically cover.</p>
</overview>

